\begin_layout Subsubsection
Special Actions in the Context Menu of the Java and BeanShell/Groovy Editor
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The context menu of the BeanShell/Groovy editor and the Java editor offers
 some methods for editing the source and for source conversions.
 These are (beside the regular actions of the platform):
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Add Block Comment
\series default
: Surrounds the selected code with a block comment.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Remove Block Comment
\series default
: Removes a selected block comment.
 (A precise selection is necessary!).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Format Java
\series default
: Formats regular Java code (To work with BeanShell or Groovy please create
 Java code inside the BeanShell/Groovy editor!).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Format selected Java
\series default
: Formats only the selected code.
 This is sometimes necessary if the formatter can not format the entire
 code.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
R Source Conversion
\series default
: Converts Rscript code.
 This converter helps to convert R expressions for the use e.g.
 in an BeanShell or Groovy script using the Rserve API.
 
\end_layout

