\begin_layout Subsection*
5.1.5 The Flow Editor
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Flow editor of the Bio7 application is capable to handle and execute
 different files by their extension and display and arrange them in a flowchart
 like structure.The Flow editor is useful to:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
It can be used to create complex sensitivity analysis for created models
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
It can serve as a guide for complex analysis of all tools offered by Bio7.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Or it simply can be used to visualize complex workflows.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The main strength of this tool is that you can assemble all methods and
 information, created by files for modeling, statistical analysis or image
 analysis in a profound analysis.
 The Flow editor of Bio7 helps to organize and visualize the creation and
 analysis of ecological models.
 A flowchart by definition is a graphic representation of a sequence of
 operations.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float figure
wide false
sideways false
status collapsed

\begin_layout Plain Layout
