\begin_layout Subsubsection
The Palette of the Flow Editor
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For the creation of a running flowchart it is necessary to create a start
 and a stop element in the flowchart.
 By activating an element in the 
\series bold
Palette
\series default
 these elements can be placed anywhere in the flowchart with the mouse at
 the appropriate coordinates (pressing mouse button will drop the component).
 Additionally when an element has been placed in the flow it can be dragged
 to any coordinates in the flow panel.
 All other elements in the 
\series bold
Palette
\series default
 can be placed by this procedure too.
 The following elements are available and their values can be adjusted in
 the 
\series bold
Properties
\series default
 view.
 Furthermore some properties can be changed directly in the shape (mouse
 click on the element) The following elements are available:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Start
\series default
 : The start of the flow - necessary for execution !
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Stop
\series default
 : The end of the flow - necessary for execution !
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Loop
\series default
 : A loop will repeat a sequence in the flowchart.
 The number of iterations can be adjusted with an integer value directly
 in the shape (click and hold ca.
 one second to edit).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Decision
\series default
 : A decision in the flow will execute an if statement.
 According to a self defined condition a static variable (Bio7Flow.setDecision(“t
rue”)) can be set to true or false.
 The direction of the flow then depends on the linked connection which can
 be set to true or false in the properties dialog (select the connections
 to set the values).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Info
\series default
 : A single line label for an info which can be edited in the shape.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Connection
\series default
: To determine the sequence of the flow 
\series bold
Connections
\series default
 are available to connect components.
 If selected in the Palette directed connections can be drawn from component
 to component.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Selections
\series default
 can be made with the 
\series bold
Marquee
\series default
 tool and the 
\series bold
Select
\series default
 tool (multiple selections are possible).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset

Options for the Layout
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
There are several tools available for adjusting the components and the layout
 of the flow.
 In the toolbar of Bio7 several items will be enabled when components are
 selected alone or in a group.
 By default the zoom action and the flow action are enabled.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
With the
\series bold
 Zoom In, Out
\series default
 actions it is possible to zoom in or to zoom out in the flow (by using
 the combo box or the lens items).
 If an opened flow was changed, the toolbar items for undo and redo could
 be used to undo or redo changes in the flow.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Furthermore components can be deleted with the
\series bold
 Delete
\series default
 item and so removed from the flow (or by pressing the delete key).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
If more than one component is selected the alignment actions (
\series bold
Align Width
\series default
, etc.) and the 
\series bold
Match Width/Height
\series default
 actions will be available to align shapes to the first selected shape or
 adjust the width or the height of selected shapes to the properties of
 the first selected component.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Additionally the added menu 
\series bold
Flowaction
\series default
 in the menubar of Bio7 offers three further options for the alignment and
 layout of the components.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
When the option Rulers is selected and marked rulers in the flow will be
 made visible for the exact layout of the flow components.
 By dragging horizontal and vertical lines from the ruler (like it is known
 from image software) components can easily be aligned to the visible ruler
 lines.
 The alignment will be supported by artificial lines (red lines) which occur
 when the alignment criteria are met.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
The option 
\series bold
Grid
\series default
 will enable a grid in the flow.
 When enabled, the components can be arranged in discrete coordinate steps
 according to the default grid size in the flow.
 Furthermore artificial lines will occur (green lines) with the enabled
 option 
\series bold
Snap to Geometry
\series default
 when a translated component matches the alignment of another component
 in the flow.
 The grid size can be adjusted in the context menu of the Flow editor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset

The Context Menu
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The context menu offers some of the aforementioned methods and several new
 methods.
 The new methods are:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The options 
\series bold
Manhatten Router
\series default
 and 
\series bold
Shortest Path
\series default
 action are responsible for the layout of the connections.
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
The Shortest Path action applies the shortest path algorithm to find paths
 around obstacles in the flow.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The Manhatten Router algorithm will use rectangular lines for connections
 in the flow.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
Save
\series default
 action will save the current flow to the before defined file (Save as in
 the Bio7 main menu available!).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
Save Image
\series default
 action will save an image in the formats *.gif*, *.jpeg, *.ico to a file.
 The current size of the flow will determine the pic size (the rulers display
 the size of the flow in pixel.
 So be cautious not to store large images with a resized flow !).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
Debug Mode
\series default
 option enables a visualization of the current flow by colouring the active
 shape white to mark files that are currently interpreted or compiled, etc.
 A mouse-click on the flow deletes marked components.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Size Layout Grid
\series default
 opens a dialog to resize the grid (layout) if enabled.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset

The Properties for the Components
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If a shape or a connection is activated the properties of the component
 or the connection can be adjusted in the 
\series bold
Properties
\series default
 view.
 This view is activated by default below the Flow editor or can be activated
 with the 
\series bold
\noun on
Windows \SpecialChar \menuseparator
Show View
\series default
\noun default
 menu action.
 The properties dialog will only be necessary if you want create a decision
 inside a flow.
 All other component attributes are adjustable with the mouse.
 The following properties are displayed and can be adjusted:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The 
\series bold
File/Loop/Info/Condition
\series default
 property displays the following attributes in dependence of the selected
 component:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
The filepath of a dropped component (relative path in the workspace.
 This path will be used for execution!)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The amount of loops which should be made when the loop component has been
 selected.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
An info text if the info component has been selected.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
When a decision component has been selected this property will be interpreted
 as a scripting expression in BeanShell.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
The filetype property shows the extension of the selected file, which has
 been dropped into the flow (has no effect on the other components).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The properties Height,Width, X,Y display the size of the component and the
 location inside the flow which can also be adjusted in the properties view.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
There are two properties if a connection is selected.
 
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
The property LineStyle can be set to dashed or solid (by default the style
 is solid).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The Boolean property is important when a decision is created in the flow.
 The property can be set to true or false.
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Note
\series default
: The properties File and Filetype are important for the execution of a
 file inside the flow editor! The file type information is used to select
 the appropriate interpreter or compiler.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph*
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset

What to Consider when Creating a Flow
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
It should be mentioned that some rules are important for the creation of
 a regular flow in the Flow editor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
A start and a stop component have to be placed in the flow and they have
 to be connected with the components for a regular Bio7 flow.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
A flow follows the outgoing direction (directed graph) marked with an outgoing
 arrowhead.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Files: 
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
A dropped file in the flow editor (rectangular shape) can only be connected
 with another file or by means of a loop which connects on or two files.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
A file component has to have one outgoing connection.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Files in the flow editor will be executed sequently by means of the information
 in the file property and the filetype property (the appropriate interpreter
 or program will be selected automatically).
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
Loops:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
A loop can have one incoming and one outgoing connection.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
A loop cannot be the first component (after the start) in a Bio7 flow.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
It is possible to execute a loop with one file component.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Loops can be created nested.
 The loops are executed “iteratively” (not “recursive” !).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
A loop can be connected (point) to a decision .
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
Decisions:
\end_layout

\begin_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
A decision gets an input from a component and has to have two outgoing connectio
ns.
 One connection has to be set to false and the other has to be set to true.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
A decision can be connected to another decision (else if).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
A decision cannot be connected (point) directly to a loop.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
It is allowed in Bio7 to place a decision right after the start.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
The condition of a decision component can be set directly in the properties
 view or in the component itself.
 The static variable decision has to be set to "true" or "false" (type:
 String) to follow a connection with the appropriate value - (API method:
 BatchModel.setDecision(“true”);).
\end_layout

\end_deeper
\begin_layout Enumerate
Info: An info component can be placed outside the connected flow for an
 information display.
 It is also allowed to draw connections to a file component as a pointer
 (optionally you can mark this connection with a changed line style).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
How to Cancel a Flow!
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
A running flow can be interrupted at the next possible flow position with
 the 
\series bold
Cancel
\series default
 action in the progress dialog (the dialog is only displayed for long operations
) or by selecting the key combination Ctrl+x (short and long operations).
 If R is used in some operations it makes sense to start Rserve with a system
 console (see 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "subsec:Rserve-preferences"

\end_inset

) before executing a flow.
 Only with a shell it is possible to interrupt an R calculation - if supported
 by the package creator.
 In some cases where the application Rserve is involved it can become necessary
 to stop and restart the application (this can be done with the Rserve connectio
n action in the toolbar of Bio7).
 If possible it is highly recommend to test all files before they are used
 in the flow editor.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset

Dropped from the Project Explorer
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Flow editor recognizes several different file types.
 Files, created with the Bio7 editors, will be executed in the flow with
 the appropriate interpreter or the embedded compiler (e.g.
 *.bsh, *.java, *.py, *.r, *.txt, *.ecor).
 Additionally the Flow editor will also execute *.exe files.
 Files with the extension *.argument can be created and dropped before the
 *.exe file in the flow sequence.
 This will execute the dropped program with an argument (xxx -argument).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset

Dropped from Outside the Project Explorer
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Files dropped from outside the navigator, will be opened or executed with
 the registered program of the operating system !
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset

Important to Know
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The dropped file components in the flow can be opened and edited with a
 double-click on that component.
 A static variable is available to trigger the flow interrupt - Bio7 method:
 Bio7Flow.setCancel(true) .
 Please consult the Bio7 API and examples for more reusable flow methods
 and components.
 
\end_layout

